## DBsubject(Mechanics)
## DBchapter(Oscillatory Motion and Waves)
## DBsection(Simple Harmonic Motion: A Special Periodic Motion)
## Date(December 2017)
## Institution(Brock University)
## Author(Brandon Lostracco)
## Edited (Connor Wilson, May, 1, 2018)
## TitleText1('College Physics')
## AuthorText1('Urone et. al')
## EditionText1('2017')
## Section1('16.')
## Problem1('')
## KEYWORDS(frequency, period, equilibrium, force, harmonic, Hooke's, Newton, law, spring)

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$mass      = random(5.00, 10.00, 0.1);
$stretch1  = random(0.2,  0.3,   0.05);
$Amplitude = random(0.1,  0.2,   0.05);

$A1 = ($mass) * (9.80) / ($stretch1);
$A2 = 2 * pi * (($mass) / $A1)**(1 / 2);
$A3 = ($Amplitude) * (($A1) / ($mass))**(1 / 2);

BEGIN_PGML
>>[!  A baby in a hanging harness. !]{'NU_U17-16-03-008.png'}{300} <<

A child bounces in a harness suspended from a door frame by a spring constant.

a)  If the spring stretches [`[$stretch1]`] [`\textrm{m}`] while supporting an [`[$mass]`]-[`\textrm{kg}`] child, what is its spring constant? 

    [_]{$A1}  [`\textrm{N/m}`]

b) What is the time for one complete bounce of this child? 

    [_]{$A1} [`\textrm{s}`]

c) What is the child's maximum velocity if the amplitude of her bounce is [`[$Amplitude]`] [`\textrm{m}`]? 

    [_]{$A3} [`\textrm{m/s}`]

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
a) The spring is stretched by its equilibrium distance when the child's weight and the spring force are balanced.

b) In other words, find the period of the child's oscillation.

c) Recall that the child will attain their maximum velocity as they traverse the equilibrium position, the point at which the mechanical energy of the child-harness system is entirely kinetic.
END_PGML_HINT

ENDDOCUMENT();
